|* Post-layout ro_array_core: the whole entropy source (four non-identical
|* rings + four output buffers + the three-xor2 combining tree), extracted
|* FLAT from ONE `klt extract --parasitics` run over
|* layout/ro_array_core-placement-poc/ro_array_core_signal9_poc.gds -- the
|* same DRC-clean (0 violations), klt-lvs-MATCHING (132/132 devices, 96/96
|* nets against design/ro_array_core.spice's own .subckt ro_array_core) GDS
|* that PoC directory's own README documents ("Increment 8"). Real inter-ring
|* wiring is included for the first time: the ring->buffer signal chain, the
|* buffer->XOR fan-in, the XOR combining tree's own t1/t2 routing, and the
|* array-wide vdd bus for the four buffers + three xor2 instances -- none of
|* which sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/ (one ring at a time, ideal
|* wires between rings) could include, and none of which
|* sim/ro-array-core-combining/ (pre-layout, no physical interconnect at
|* all) could include either.
|*
|* Purpose (issue #22's acceptance bar: "Post-layout PVT simulation results
|* land under sim/, extracted parasitics included" plus the DR-0003 section
|* 8 wstv inter-ring decorrelation re-evaluation). This is a two-way,
|* same-corner comparison (post-layout array vs. pre-layout control, the
|* SAME topology sim/ro-array-core-combining/'s own testbench drives),
|* matching sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/'s own comparison discipline
|* one hierarchy level up. It reuses that record's own measurement set
|* (per-ring periods, combining fidelity in both the edge-retention and
|* value-fidelity senses, and array supply current) rather than inventing a
|* new one, so every number here is directly comparable to
|* sim/ro-array-core-combining/'s own pre-layout record by name.
|*
|* Topology, post-layout side (prefix p): xarr is ONE flat-extracted cell --
|* design/xschem/ro_array_core.sch's own hierarchy, already wired, sourced
|* from layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice via
|* layout/bin/pex-netlist.py (shared, unmodified, with
|* layout/pex/pex.json's and layout/pex-ring/pex.json's own leaf/ring
|* descriptors). t1/t2 (the XOR tree's own inter-stage nets) are internal to
|* the wrapper subckt at the SAME literal names design/ro_array_core.spice's
|* own .subckt ro_array_core uses internally, so they are reachable exactly
|* the way sim/ro-array-core-combining/'s own testbench reaches them
|* (`v(xarr.t1)`, one level of hierarchy) -- confirmed by this deck's own
|* first successful run, not assumed.
|*
|* Topology, pre-layout side (no prefix, matching
|* sim/ro-array-core-combining/'s own testbench net names exactly): xctl is
|* the identical topology from design/ro_array_core.spice's parameterized
|* .subckt ro_array_core, same-deck same-corner control.
|*
|* The substrate tie. layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice declares the
|* extractor's substrate return node `vsubs` .global (klayout-tools#1503,
|* same as every other post-layout deck in this repo). This deck ties it
|* HARD to 0, the same physically-motivated choice
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/ and sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/ both
|* use -- every composed cell's own psub guard ring is tied to vss, and vss
|* is 0 here. Inter-ring coupling through a floating substrate is a
|* different, separately-bracketed question (spec/decision-records/DR-0005)
|* and is not re-litigated by this deck's own hard tie.
|*
|* PVT: the same four (temp, supply) points
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/ uses, each bundling the tt/ss/ff
|* process axis:
|*   -40 degC / 1.62 V   the measured entropy-binding corner (ss)
|*    27 degC / 1.80 V   nominal
|*   125 degC / 1.98 V   the worst five-stage ring swing in #10's grid
|*   -40 degC / 1.98 V   the fastest ring measured anywhere in that grid
|*
|* Window. Post-layout parasitics measurably slow the array (every prior
|* post-layout ring record in this repo reports 1.4x-2.4x slowdown over
|* pre-layout, and the array adds inter-ring wiring + XOR-tree loading on
|* top), so this deck's tstop is 4x sim/ro-array-core-combining/'s own 200n
|* -- 800n -- with the same 5 ns enable-release point and the same
|* 10-period ring / 48-edge combining-node estimators (rise=3..13 for
|* periods, rise=2..50 at the combining nodes), now measured from a 700 ns
|* window (100 ns to 800 ns) rather than that deck's 60-200 ns, to keep the
|* same edge counts reachable at the slowest corner. Confirmed sufficient by
|* this deck's own first run at every corner (every meas below resolved,
|* not "no value found"), not assumed from the pre-layout deck's own margin.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* tt, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/ro_array_core.spice, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice, 125.0, 1.98 and 5p. As
|* committed it is not a runnable deck. Invoke with
|* `--ro-ring5 design/ro_array_core.spice` and
|* `--pex-lib layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice`.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" tt
|
|* pre-layout subcircuit library (ro_array_core / ro_ring5 / ro_buf / xor2)
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/ro_array_core.spice"
|* post-layout ARRAY subcircuit library (ro_array_core_pex, flat-extracted
|* from the whole composed, DRC-clean and LVS-clean array GDS)
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice"
|
|.temp 125.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: hard tie (see header) ----------------------
|Vsub vsubs 0 dc 0
|
|* --- post-layout ARRAY, one flat-extracted cell for the whole block ----
|Vddrp1 pvddr1 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp2 pvddr2 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp3 pvddr3 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp4 pvddr4 0 dc 1.98
|Vddp pvdd 0 dc 1.98
|Venp1 pen1 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Venp2 pen2 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Venp3 pen3 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Venp4 pen4 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|xarr pen1 pen2 pen3 pen4 pvddr1 pvddr2 pvddr3 pvddr4 pvdd 0 pxo pro1 pro2 pro3 pro4 ro_array_core_pex
|
|* --- pre-layout control, identical topology, single-call subckt --------
|Vddr1 vddr1 0 dc 1.98
|Vddr2 vddr2 0 dc 1.98
|Vddr3 vddr3 0 dc 1.98
|Vddr4 vddr4 0 dc 1.98
|Vdd vdd 0 dc 1.98
|Ven1 en1 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Ven2 en2 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Ven3 en3 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Ven4 en4 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|xctl en1 en2 en3 en4 vddr1 vddr2 vddr3 vddr4 vdd 0 xo ro1 ro2 ro3 ro4 ro_array_core
|
|.ic v(pro1)=0
|.ic v(pro2)=0
|.ic v(pro3)=0
|.ic v(pro4)=0
|.ic v(ro1)=0
|.ic v(ro2)=0
|.ic v(ro3)=0
|.ic v(ro4)=0
|
|* Limit the saved transient trace set to exactly what the .meas statements
|* below need. Without this, ngspice keeps a full-resolution voltage history
|* for every node in the deck -- including every per-terminal parasitic-star
|* leg node the flat ARRAY extraction introduces (132 devices' worth, an
|* order of magnitude more than one ring alone) -- and
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/'s own header records this exhausting
|* process memory outright at the ff corner's shorter timesteps. None of
|* those internal leg voltages are read by any .meas below.
|.save v(pro1) v(pro2) v(pro3) v(pro4) v(pxo) v(xarr.t1)
|.save v(ro1) v(ro2) v(ro3) v(ro4) v(xo) v(xctl.t1)
|.save i(Vddrp1) i(Vddrp2) i(Vddrp3) i(Vddrp4) i(Vddp)
|.save i(Vddr1) i(Vddr2) i(Vddr3) i(Vddr4) i(Vdd)
|
|.tran 5p 800n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|* --- post-layout ARRAY: per-ring periods, 10 whole periods each, first
|* two rising edges discarded as start-up ------------------------------
|meas tran pt1a when v(pro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt1b when v(pro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr1 = (pt1b - pt1a)/10
|meas tran pt2a when v(pro2)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt2b when v(pro2)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr2 = (pt2b - pt2a)/10
|meas tran pt3a when v(pro3)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt3b when v(pro3)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr3 = (pt3b - pt3a)/10
|meas tran pt4a when v(pro4)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt4b when v(pro4)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr4 = (pt4b - pt4a)/10
|let p_f_ideal2 = 1/p_tr1 + 1/p_tr2
|let p_f_ideal = 1/p_tr1 + 1/p_tr2 + 1/p_tr3 + 1/p_tr4
|let p_skew_span = p_tr1/p_tr4
|
|* --- post-layout ARRAY combining node: swing and realized edge rate ---
|meas tran pvxo_max MAX v(pxo) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran pvxo_min MIN v(pxo) from=100n to=800n
|let p_swing_frac_xo = (pvxo_max - pvxo_min) / 1.98
|meas tran ptxo_a when v(pxo)=0.5*1.98 rise=2
|meas tran ptxo_b when v(pxo)=0.5*1.98 rise=50
|let p_f_xo = 48/(ptxo_b - ptxo_a)
|let p_edge_retention = p_f_xo / p_f_ideal
|meas tran ptt1a when v(xarr.t1)=0.5*1.98 rise=2
|meas tran ptt1b when v(xarr.t1)=0.5*1.98 rise=50
|let p_f_t1 = 48/(ptt1b - ptt1a)
|let p_retention_n2 = p_f_t1 / p_f_ideal2
|let p_retention_n4 = p_edge_retention
|
|* --- post-layout ARRAY value fidelity + supply current -----------------
|meas tran pvxo_avg AVG v(pxo) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran pvt1_avg AVG v(xarr.t1) from=100n to=800n
|let p_bias_xo = pvxo_avg / 1.98
|let p_bias_t1 = pvt1_avg / 1.98
|meas tran pi1 AVG i(Vddrp1) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran pi2 AVG i(Vddrp2) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran pi3 AVG i(Vddrp3) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran pi4 AVG i(Vddrp4) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran pib AVG i(Vddp) from=100n to=800n
|let p_i_rings = -(pi1 + pi2 + pi3 + pi4)
|let p_i_block = -pib
|let p_i_array_total = p_i_rings + p_i_block
|let p_p_array_total = p_i_array_total * 1.98
|
|* --- pre-layout CONTROL: identical estimators, identical node names as
|* sim/ro-array-core-combining/'s own testbench ---------------------------
|meas tran t1a when v(ro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran t1b when v(ro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let tr1 = (t1b - t1a)/10
|meas tran t2a when v(ro2)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran t2b when v(ro2)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let tr2 = (t2b - t2a)/10
|meas tran t3a when v(ro3)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran t3b when v(ro3)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let tr3 = (t3b - t3a)/10
|meas tran t4a when v(ro4)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran t4b when v(ro4)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let tr4 = (t4b - t4a)/10
|let f_ideal2 = 1/tr1 + 1/tr2
|let f_ideal = 1/tr1 + 1/tr2 + 1/tr3 + 1/tr4
|let skew_span = tr1/tr4
|
|meas tran vxo_max MAX v(xo) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran vxo_min MIN v(xo) from=100n to=800n
|let swing_frac_xo = (vxo_max - vxo_min) / 1.98
|meas tran txo_a when v(xo)=0.5*1.98 rise=2
|meas tran txo_b when v(xo)=0.5*1.98 rise=50
|let f_xo = 48/(txo_b - txo_a)
|let edge_retention = f_xo / f_ideal
|meas tran tt1a when v(xctl.t1)=0.5*1.98 rise=2
|meas tran tt1b when v(xctl.t1)=0.5*1.98 rise=50
|let f_t1 = 48/(tt1b - tt1a)
|let retention_n2 = f_t1 / f_ideal2
|let retention_n4 = edge_retention
|
|meas tran vxo_avg AVG v(xo) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran vt1_avg AVG v(xctl.t1) from=100n to=800n
|let bias_xo = vxo_avg / 1.98
|let bias_t1 = vt1_avg / 1.98
|meas tran i1 AVG i(Vddr1) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran i2 AVG i(Vddr2) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran i3 AVG i(Vddr3) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran i4 AVG i(Vddr4) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran ib AVG i(Vdd) from=100n to=800n
|let i_rings = -(i1 + i2 + i3 + i4)
|let i_block = -ib
|let i_array_total = i_rings + i_block
|let p_array_total_pre = i_array_total * 1.98
|
|* --- headline ratios: same block, same corner, real inter-ring wiring
|* (plus real intra-cell parasitics) vs. pre-layout (no interconnect,
|* ideal devices only) ----------------------------------------------------
|let slowdown_r1 = p_tr1 / tr1
|let slowdown_r2 = p_tr2 / tr2
|let slowdown_r3 = p_tr3 / tr3
|let slowdown_r4 = p_tr4 / tr4
|
|print p_tr1
|print p_tr2
|print p_tr3
|print p_tr4
|print p_skew_span
|print p_f_ideal
|print p_f_xo
|print p_edge_retention
|print p_retention_n2
|print p_retention_n4
|print p_bias_t1
|print p_bias_xo
|print p_swing_frac_xo
|print p_i_rings
|print p_i_block
|print p_i_array_total
|print p_p_array_total
|print tr1
|print tr2
|print tr3
|print tr4
|print skew_span
|print f_ideal
|print f_xo
|print edge_retention
|print retention_n2
|print retention_n4
|print bias_t1
|print bias_xo
|print swing_frac_xo
|print i_rings
|print i_block
|print i_array_total
|print p_array_total_pre
|print slowdown_r1
|print slowdown_r2
|print slowdown_r3
|print slowdown_r4
|.endc
|.end
|

